# Niuma environment template
# Copy to the repo root as .env.local (gitignored). Relative paths are resolved
# from the directory that contains that file. The Tauri build also reads
# .env.local / .env from the repo root via src-tauri/build.rs.
#
# Do not put real secrets in this file. Do not commit .env.local.

# --- Local content roots ----------------------------------------------------
# Preferred: the project root that contains .teams/
NIUMA_CONTENT_DIR=.
NIUMA_ARTIFACT_DIR=./.artifacts

# --- Frontend (Vite, optional) ---------------------------------------------
# VITE_ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# --- IMA OpenAPI (content team / 文章资产) ---------------------------------
# Same names as ima-skill. Aliases IMA_CLIENT_ID / IMA_API_KEY also work.
# IMA_OPENAPI_CLIENTID=
# IMA_OPENAPI_APIKEY=

# --- WeChat official accounts (content team /publish WECHAT) ---------------
# Add WECHAT_2_* … for extra slots. APPSECRET must never be pasted into chat.
# WECHAT_1_NAME=
# WECHAT_1_APPID=
# WECHAT_1_APPSECRET=

# --- Optional local API keys (Settings can also store these) ---------------
# STT_API_KEY=
# AGNES_API_KEY=
# UNSPLASH_ACCESS_KEY=

# --- Compiled into the Tauri binary (src-tauri/build.rs) -------------------
# Leave empty to disable. Only needed for production / license-gated builds.
# POSTHOG_API_KEY=
# PAYMENT_ENDPOINT=
# API_ACCESS_KEY=
# APP_ENDPOINT=

# --- GitHub Actions (repo Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions) ------
# These are not copied into .env.local. The Release workflow reads them as
# repository secrets so `push` to main/master publishes a GitHub Release:
#   GITHUB_TOKEN                      — provided by Actions; needs contents: write
#   TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY         — minisign private key (updater .sig)
#   TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD
# Generate a keypair: npx @tauri-apps/cli signer generate -w ~/.tauri/niuma.key
# Put the public key in src-tauri/tauri.conf.json → plugins.updater.pubkey
